**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** Licence attribution is a fact of an entry's provenance, decided once in Domain (001 §B 'Licence attribution: CC-BY entries show their attribution in the Library and Materials windows and in the Details view'; the S3.3 brief: an entry whose provenance licence requires attribution shows its citation, and CC0 shows the licence name only). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`, after `EntryProvenance` and `EntryForkInfo` (steps 24, 91), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S3.3: (1) `EntryAttribution` = `LicenceAndCitation of licence : EntryLicence * citation : EntryCitation` | `LicenceNameOnly of licence : EntryLicence` is what an entry shows about its licence. Its `member this.text : string` is the honest render (ELEV002): `Licence <licence> — cite: <citation>` and `Licence <licence>`. (2) `type EntryLicence with member this.attributionWith (citation : EntryCitation) : EntryAttribution` holds the one CC-BY rule. A licence whose SPDX identifier starts with `CC-BY` (`StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`: `CC-BY-4.0`, `CC-BY-SA-4.0`, `CC-BY-NC-4.0` …) obliges its user to credit the source, so it answers `LicenceAndCitation`. Every other licence, `CC0-1.0` included, answers `LicenceNameOnly`. No other licence family, table or option is added. (3) `type EntryProvenance with member this.attributionOpt : EntryAttribution option`. `SourcePullProvenance info` answers `Some (info.licence.attributionWith info.citation)`. `ForkProvenance fork` answers `fork.originalProvenance.attributionOpt`, so a fork of a pulled entry, and a fork of that fork, keep its credit (S3.1 interpretation 2). `BuiltInProvenance`, `UserProvenance` and `KitImportProvenance` answer `None`, because they carry no licence. (4) `EntryAttributionLine = { entryName : EntryName; attribution : EntryAttribution }` is one credited entry as a surface lists it, with `member this.text : string` = `<entry name>: <attribution text>`. (5) `type LibraryEntry with member this.attributedEntryIds : LibraryEntryId list` names the entries a surface showing the entry credits: the entry's own id (`entry.entryId.tryToLibraryEntryId`, step 24; none for a non-GUID id), then, for a `SampleItem`, every material its structure references (`ElementId.fs:188` `SampleStructure.referencedMaterials`) through `MaterialId.toLibraryEntryId`, in that set's order. A sample's own provenance carries no licence, but the optical constants of its layers may. (6) The fixture `OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs` (step 41, linked into the UI suite) gains, each with a one-line doc, the builders both suites use for licensed and user entries, so no fact copies them. `licensedMaterialContent (id : MaterialId) (name : EntryName) (licence : EntryLicence) (citation : EntryCitation) : LibraryEntryContent` is the catalogue's Silicon (`MaterialIds.silicon`, decoded from `catalogueData ()`) under `id` and `name`, built with `LibraryEntryContent.ofMaterialEntry VersionNumber.first` under `SourcePullProvenance { source = MaterialSourceName "Test optical constants"; record = MaterialSourceRecordId "test/<name>"; sourceVersion = MaterialSourceVersion "2026-11-01"; licence = licence; citation = citation }`. `userMaterialContent (id : MaterialId) (name : EntryName) : LibraryEntryContent` is the same Silicon under `UserProvenance`. `userCategoryContent (id : CategoryId) (name : CategoryName) : LibraryEntryContent` is the catalogue's Glass category (`CategoryIds.glass`) under `id`, `name` and `UserCategory`, built with `ofMaterialCategory VersionNumber.first UserProvenance`. `sampleContentOver (id : SampleId) (material : MaterialId) (name : EntryName) : LibraryEntryContent` is the catalogue's `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` sample under `id`, `name` and `UserProvenance`, its films replaced by one 100 nm `SingleLayer` of version 1 of `material`. `putSealedEntries (context : CatalogueImportContext) (contents : LibraryEntryContent list) : unit` seals each content through `context.sealEntry` and puts it through `context.proxy.putEntryVersion` with `MoveLatestVersion`, in order. A builder or seam error fails the calling fact with its `describe`. (7) Tests, in `LibraryEntryFilesTests`. `a CC-BY licence attributes with its citation and any other licence by its name alone`: `CC-BY-4.0`, `cc-by-sa-4.0` and `CC-BY-NC-4.0` answer `LicenceAndCitation`, `CC0-1.0` and `MIT` answer `LicenceNameOnly`, and the two texts are exactly `Licence CC-BY-4.0 — cite: <citation>` and `Licence CC0-1.0`. `a pulled entry and its forks carry its licence's attribution, and every other provenance none`: a `SourcePullProvenance` under `CC-BY-4.0`, a fork of it and a fork of that fork answer the same `LicenceAndCitation`; a `SourcePullProvenance` under `CC0-1.0` answers `LicenceNameOnly`; `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`, `UserProvenance` and a `KitImportProvenance` of a test-local `KitId` answer `None`; and an `EntryAttributionLine` named `PTB glass` renders `PTB glass: <its attribution's text>`. `an entry's attributed ids are its own and its sample's materials`: a source preset of the catalogue answers its own id alone, and the `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` sample answers its own id followed by `MaterialIds.glass152` and `MaterialIds.vacuumMaterial` in the order of its `referencedMaterials`.

**Acceptance.** After the attribution lands, `EntryProvenance.attributionOpt` MUST answer a pulled entry's licence attribution, through any fork, and `None` for every other provenance; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a CC-BY licence attributes with its citation and any other licence by its name alone`, `a pulled entry and its forks carry its licence's attribution, and every other provenance none`, `an entry's attributed ids are its own and its sample's materials`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.
